          <h1>Roofing Questions, Answered Honestly</h1>
          <p>These answers are general information, not a promise of specific pricing, warranty terms, or insurance outcomes. Your written estimate controls.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-list">
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">How much does roof replacement cost? <i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i></button>
            <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Cost depends on roof size, pitch, material, number of tear-off layers, decking condition, flashing details, ventilation, permits, and local labor rates. National averages vary widely: many asphalt shingle replacements fall in the range of roughly $8,500 to $16,000 for a typical single-family home, with some projects lower and some higher. Metal roofing typically costs more. We provide a written, itemized estimate after inspecting your roof—not a phone quote based on guessing.</div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">How long does roof installation take? <i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i></button>
            <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">For a standard asphalt shingle roof, most residential replacements take about 1 to 3 days on site, assuming good weather and a single-layer tear-off. Metal roofing often takes 2 to 5 days, and standing seam may take 3 to 7 days depending on complexity. Larger roofs, steep pitches, multiple layers, or decking repairs add time. Your written scope will include an expected schedule.</div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">When should I replace my roof? <i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i></button>
            <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Age alone is not the only factor. Signs that warrant an inspection include missing or curling shingles, granules in gutters, visible flashing damage, ceiling stains, attic moisture, sagging, and repeated leaks. Asphalt shingles often last 15 to 40 years depending on product, climate, ventilation, and maintenance. A professional inspection can tell you whether repair or replacement makes more sense.</div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Do you offer free roof inspections? <i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i></button>
            <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes. We offer free, no-obligation roof inspections for homeowners and property managers. The inspection documents visible conditions and helps you understand options. It does not obligate you to hire us.</div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Do you handle storm damage? <i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i></button>
            <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">We assess wind and hail damage and provide detailed repair or replacement estimates. We can document damage and provide a written scope you can share with your insurer. We do not act as a public adjuster, we do not submit insurance claims on your behalf, and we do not guarantee any insurance outcome. You choose your contractor and file your own claim.</div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">What roofing materials do you install? <i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i></button>
            <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">We install asphalt shingle systems (3-tab and architectural), metal roofing (standing seam and metal shingles), and low-slope commercial systems where offered. Material availability varies by region and project. Manufacturer warranties vary by product and installation requirements. Ask for the specific product data sheet and warranty terms in your estimate.</div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Are financing options available? <i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i></button>
