          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">What should I check before hiring a roofing contractor? <i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i></button>
            <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Verify the contractor’s license and insurance where required by your state or municipality. Ask for a written contract that includes scope, materials, payment schedule, and cancellation terms. Be cautious of high-pressure “now-or-never” offers, demands for large cash deposits, or contractors who offer to “handle” your insurance claim for you. The FTC’s Cooling-Off Rule gives you three business days to cancel certain door-to-door sales of $25 or more, and many states have additional protections.</div></div>
